# TikTok API SDK for Python

[![PyPI version](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/{{ project_name }}?color=0274b5)](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![PyPI downloads](https://img.shields.io/pypi/dm/{{ project_name }})](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![Python versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/{{ project_name }})](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](https://github.com/EulerStream/TikTok-Api-Sdk/blob/master/LICENSE)
[![Discord](https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-join-5865F2)](https://www.eulerstream.com/discord)

`{{ project_name }}` is the official Python client for the [EulerStream TikTok API](https://www.eulerstream.com). Use one typed TikTok API client, sync or async, to **look up TikTok users and videos**, run **TikTok OAuth**, **sign TikTok web requests** and **solve TikTok captchas**. The complete TikTok LIVE API is included as well, so the same client can read real-time LIVE chat, gifts and viewer counts.

The TikTok API behind this SDK is hosted by EulerStream, the managed TikTok backend behind [TikTokLive](https://github.com/isaackogan/TikTokLive), the most popular Python library for TikTok LIVE. Request signing, captcha solving and the LIVE connection layer are maintained for you, so your integration keeps working when TikTok changes.

> Unofficial: this project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to TikTok or ByteDance.

Only need TikTok LIVE? [`tiktok-live-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-live-api-sdk/) is the same client with just the LIVE groups.

## Installation

```bash
pip install {{ project_name }}
```

Requires Python 3.11+. Built on [httpx](https://www.python-httpx.org/) and [attrs](https://www.attrs.org/); every endpoint has `sync`, `sync_detailed`, `asyncio` and `asyncio_detailed` variants and ships with full type hints (`py.typed`).

## TikTok API quick start

1. [Create a free EulerStream account](https://www.eulerstream.com/register) (no credit card required)
2. Copy your API key from the dashboard
3. Make your first TikTok API calls:

```python
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_videos import retrieve_tik_tok_video_basic
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_live import retrieve_hashtag_list

client = AuthenticatedClient(base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com", token="YOUR_API_KEY")

with client as c:
    # TikTok users API: look up any TikTok user by @username
    user = retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic.sync(unique_id="tv_asahi_news", client=c)
    print(user.user.nickname)

    # TikTok videos API: look up a TikTok video by its ID
    video = retrieve_tik_tok_video_basic.sync(video_id="7318296342189919018", client=c)
    print(video.message)

    # TikTok LIVE API (included): list the hashtags LIVE streams are grouped under
    hashtags = retrieve_hashtag_list.sync(client=c)
    print(hashtags.message)
```

The same TikTok API calls with asyncio:

```python
import asyncio
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic

async def main():
    async with AuthenticatedClient(base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com", token="YOUR_API_KEY") as c:
        user = await retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic.asyncio(unique_id="tv_asahi_news", client=c)
        print(user.user.nickname)

asyncio.run(main())
```

`AuthenticatedClient` sends your key in the `X-Api-Key` header; use `{{ package_name }}.Client` for the handful of routes that allow anonymous access.

## What the TikTok API covers

Every path/method in the [EulerStream OpenAPI spec](https://www.eulerstream.com/docs/openapi) becomes a module under `{{ package_name }}.api.<group>`, so the SDK always matches the live TikTok API.

| TikTok API | Module | Functions |
|---|---|---|
| **TikTok users API** | `api.tik_tok_users` | `retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic`, `retrieve_tik_tok_user_info`, `search_tik_tok_users_catalog`, `retrieve_tik_tok_users_catalog_username`, `retrieve_tik_tok_users_catalog_numeric_id` |
| **TikTok videos API** | `api.tik_tok_videos` | `retrieve_tik_tok_video_basic`, `retrieve_tik_tok_video_detailed`, `retrieve_tik_tok_video_thumbnail` |
| **TikTok OAuth** | `api.tik_tok_general` | `exchange_token`, `introspect_token`, `revoke_token`, `validate_refresh_token`, `get_user_info`, `get_public_client` |
| **TikTok request signing** | `api.tik_tok_signing` | `sign_tik_tok_url`, plus decryptors for TikTok's encrypted payloads |
| **TikTok captcha solving** | `api.tik_tok_captchas` | `complete_puzzle_captcha`, `complete_shapes_captcha`, `complete_icon_captcha`, `complete_whirl_captcha`, `retrieve_captcha_credits` |
| **Your account** | `api.accounts` / `api.authentication` / `api.analytics` | Account details, rate limits, API keys, JWTs and usage analytics |

Per-endpoint Python examples for every TikTok API operation are in the [EulerStream API docs](https://www.eulerstream.com/docs/intro).

## TikTok LIVE API included

Everything in [`tiktok-live-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-live-api-sdk/) is part of this package too:

| Module | TikTok LIVE API group |
|---|---|
| `api.tik_tok_live` | Core TikTok LIVE: bulk live checks, webcast feed, hashtag lists, rankings |
| `api.tik_tok_live_anchors` | LIVE creators: webcast URL by `@username`, room info / ID / cover, gift gallery, earnings, moderators, LIVE analytics |
| `api.tik_tok_live_rooms` | LIVE rooms: webcast URL by room ID, room info, room gifts, send chat |
| `api.tik_tok_live_events` | TikTok LIVE event history for a creator |
| `api.tik_tok_live_gifts` | TikTok LIVE gifts: the gift list, the gift catalog, search and single-gift lookup |
| `api.tik_tok_live_rankings` | LIVE creator leaderboards, rankings and ranking history |
| `api.tik_tok_live_agencies` | TikTok LIVE agency catalog |
| `api.tik_tok_live_alerts` / `api.tik_tok_live_alert_targets` | TikTok LIVE start/end alerts and webhook targets |
| `api.tik_tok_live_moderation` | LIVE kicks, bans, mutes, sensitive words and comment toggles |
| `api.tik_tok_web_socket_api` | Your cloud WebSocket connections and their state |

## What you can build with the TikTok API

- **Creator lookups and profile tools** backed by TikTok user profiles and the users catalog
- **Video tools** that fetch TikTok video details and thumbnails by ID
- **"Sign in with TikTok" flows** using the OAuth token, introspection and revocation routes
- **Scrapers and data pipelines** that sign TikTok web requests through the API instead of maintaining signature code
- **Captcha handling** for your own TikTok automation: puzzle, shapes, icon and whirl solvers
- **Everything TikTok LIVE**: stream overlays, gift alerts, chat bots, moderation tools and LIVE monitoring

## Advanced usage

Customize the underlying `httpx.Client` / `httpx.AsyncClient` (timeouts, proxies, event hooks) through `httpx_args`, or replace it entirely:

```python
import httpx
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient

client = AuthenticatedClient(
    base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com",
    token="YOUR_API_KEY",
    timeout=httpx.Timeout(30),
    httpx_args={"proxy": "http://localhost:8030"},
)
```

See the docstrings on `Client` and `AuthenticatedClient` for every option, including `verify_ssl`, `raise_on_unexpected_status` and `follow_redirects`.

## Migrating

Coming from `EulerApiSdk`? This package is the same client with everything it had, so migrating is a package name change. Uninstall the old package first, then install this one:

```bash
pip uninstall EulerApiSdk
pip install {{ project_name }}
```

Your existing code keeps running: `import EulerApiSdk` still works and resolves to the same modules, with a `DeprecationWarning`. Switch your imports to `{{ package_name }}` when convenient. If your program imports the SDK from several threads, import `EulerApiSdk` once before starting them, or use the new name, which has no such requirement.

Uninstalling first matters: this package provides the old `EulerApiSdk` import name from the same folder the old package installed into, and pip does not notice two packages sharing a folder.

## Other languages

The TikTok API SDK is also available for [Node.js / TypeScript](https://www.npmjs.com/package/tiktok-api-sdk), [C# / .NET](https://www.nuget.org/packages/EulerApiSdk), [Java](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/com.eulerstream/euler-api-sdk) and [Go](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/EulerStream/TikTok-Live-Api/sdk/go), and anything else can call the TikTok API over plain HTTP.

